ou</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name> <article-title>A modified automated high-throughput mycobacterial interspersed repetitive unit method for genotyping <italic>Mycobacterium tuberculosis.</italic></article-title><source>Diagn Microbiol Infect Dis</source> <year>2005</year>;<volume>53</volume>:<fpage>325</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.diagmicrobio.2005.05.013</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16289635</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Aranaz</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lie&#x02019;bana</surname> <given-names>E</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Mateos</surname> <given-names>A</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Dominguez</surname> <given-names>L</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Vidal</surname> <given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Domingo</surname> <given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Spacer oligonucleotide typing of <italic>Mycobacterium bovis</italic> strains from cattle and other animals: a tool for studying epidemiology of tuberculosis.</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>1996</year>;<volume>34</volume>:<fpage>2734</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8897175</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Hsu</surname> <given-names>YH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Chen</surname> <given-names>CW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Sun</surname> <given-names>HS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Jou</surname> <given-names>R</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Lee</surname> <given-names>JJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Su</surname> <given-names>IJ</given-names></string-name> <article-titl